title: Sealed by the Spirit – The Earnest of Our Inheritance
description: Once we believe we are sealed by the Holy Spirit as the earnest until the day of redemption, that we may know we have eternal life. Built from the teachings.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-assurance-sealed-by-the-spirit.html

# Built from the "Sealed by the Spirit" teachings in studies/data/topics/assurance.json, with standalone and
# untitled-theme teachings on the same subject. Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed but not reworded.

=== The doctrine
# from 17189
--- Sealed by the Spirit [title]
overline: Doctrine · Assurance
heading: Sealed by the Spirit
sub: The only surety we can count on is God's.
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the study. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 4581, 12761
--- Sealed unto the day of redemption
big: Ephesians 1:13-14 | mark: ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise
lead: Once we believe we are sealed by the Holy Spirit as the earnest, the down payment as it were, until redemption, where God makes good on His promise, on the day of the Lord.
note: This is the promise, that we who are saved may know we are His, and that we know we have eternal life. [[Ephesians 4:30]]

=== The earnest and the surety
# from 10835
--- What the earnest is
lead: Earnest is money, sometimes called a “good faith deposit,” a sum that is included with your offer to purchase something to show your seriousness of intent to go through with the purchase, which is also called redemption.
callout: The Spirit is the earnest of God, given in Christ, sealing us as His until the resurrection, whereby we are redeemed.
refs: 1 Corinthians 6:20; Ephesians 1:14

# from 4581
--- Purchased by the blood
lead: Once you are saved you are purchased by the blood.
p: To let you know God's promise is good, He sets the Holy Spirit to seal you, to quicken your spirit, to awake the new man inside, and that seal is until the day He redeems you. He makes good on the promise. He raises you from the dead in glorified bodies to inherit His Kingdom.
callout: It is a contract entered in to by faith with God by believing His testimony. Taking Him at His word.

# from 11565
--- Christ our surety, the Spirit our earnest
fig: A surety of a better testament | Hebrews 7:22
fig: The earnest of the Spirit | 2 Corinthians 1:21-22
p: The idea of temporarily giving or using collateral to ensure keeping of a vow before God, and redemption, is reflected in salvation, where Jesus is offered, the vow made, the Spirit serving as surety until the day of redemption.
callout: And we can believe His vow, that we will be redeemed, after He gave His Son as surety and the Spirit as earnest.

# from 17189
--- The only surety we can count on
lit: He that is surety for a stranger | Proverbs 11:15 | One who disfavors backing another's debts is seen by God as more sure than one who gives their pledge for a stranger.
p: The only surety we can count on is God's. In scripture the Holy Spirit is described as the "earnest" or seal guaranteeing a believer's eternal inheritance and salvation. The surety of our eternal life.
callout: Because our surety is covered by the finished work of Christ, and sealed by the earnest payment of the Spirit, we can count on it.

=== The witness within
# from 10836, 12761, 14528
--- The Spirit beareth witness
big: Romans 8:16-17 | mark: The Spirit itself beareth witness with our spirit
p: The correct answer is the Spirit testifying within you that you have eternal life, and the spirit of adoption, whereby you cry out "Abba!" because you finally know and understand that He is your Father.
p: You have the Spirit testifying within you. You know you are saved. Sealed.

# from 10836, 10835
--- When the flesh fails
scripture: Romans 7:24-25
p: Romans 7 explains the war within the saved between the spirit and the flesh. But we are delivered from this mortal body.
callout: And if we fail, and sin and the flesh dies, we still have eternity in the same glory, that this temporary condition will be no more. So rejoice, rather than despair. We are not like those that don't believe. We know for certain our final condition.

# from 14528, 15099, 4848
--- How we know
big: 1 John 5:13 | mark: that ye may know that ye have eternal life
lead: We who are going to Heaven know we are going to Heaven because God who cannot lie promised that all who believe on Christ, that His Son Jesus died and rose again from the dead in fulfilment of scriptures, have eternal life.
center: Nothing else matters. Not what we do. Not how we feel about it. Only that He gave us His word.

# from 4848
--- Do you believe the record?
scripture: 1 John 5:10-12 | mark: God hath given to us eternal life, and this life is in his Son
panel-warn: Calling God a liar | If you think it can be lost, or must be achieved or maintained by your own works, or that it's not knowable, that you can't have confidence in this gift, then you're calling God a liar.

=== Answering the doubters
# from 2525
--- Saved Christians believe the word
lead: If you want to know if someone is a saved Christian, the evidence isn't their lifestyle or their adherence to the commandments. The only sure way to know is if they believe the word of God.
panel-warn: Fruit inspectors | You may need to see change in someone to have them justified before you, because you're a respecter of persons.
panel: Justified before God | But to be justified before God one needs only believe his testimony and accept it as truth.

# from 13942, 10667
--- Assurance is not presumption
panel-warn: The sin of presumption | One of the most pernicious and wicked damnable heresies of the Catholic church is to make faith in the Gospel into a "sin of presumption."
panel: The Spirit testifies | But we who are saved know that we have the Holy Spirit testifying within us that we are the sons of God.
p: All epistles are written to the saved. The naysayers today in the false apostate churches would charge Paul with the "sin of presumption," for assuming he is saved, let alone assuming others are. [[Romans 1:11-12]]

# from 4767
--- Work out your own salvation
lit: Work out your own salvation | Philippians 2:12 | Many works-based false teachers use the “work out your own salvation with fear and trembling” line to teach that you cannot be assured salvation, and that we must do works to be saved.
rev: He will perform it | Philippians 1:6 | He has confidence in them, that they partake in the same grace that saved him.
p: It is another case of reading the whole of scripture and comparing it with itself, saving us from bad doctrine.

# from 4663
--- Against false churches
panel: Sealed | That we are sealed by the Spirit, given eternal life, testified by the new man within us, that we may know and have confidence in our trust in God. This is the promise of salvation.
panel-warn: The bondsmen | Denominations that teach you can lose your salvation, that you must earn it, that only they can give it... these false churches cannot save. They are the bondsmen, keeping people in chains.
refs: Ephesians 4:4-6; Ephesians 4:14; Ephesians 4:30

# from 9229
--- Doubt and the report
fig: Art thou he that should come? | Luke 7:19-20
fig: Blessed is he | Luke 7:22-23
p: It is ok to have doubts. To seek a confirmation for the hope we have, but at the end of the day we are to believe the report. To trust God and His promises.

=== God's seal
# from 16154
--- God's mark and the beast's
fig: A mark upon the foreheads | Ezekiel 9:4
lit: The counterfeit | Revelation 13:16
p: This is what the beast is copying. But God has sealed us with the Spirit unto redemption. And those 144K that will come during the wrath will be likewise sealed. God protects His own.
center: Our Lord will not forsake us.

# from 17572
--- A fountain sealed
big: Song of Solomon 4:12 | mark: a fountain sealed
p: A fountain sealed, carrying the seal of the King, and so kept pure from pollution. In this allegory we see the promise of eternal security in Christ. We are eternally His.

=== Summary
# from 4581, 10835, 11565, 10836, 14528, 2525, 13942
--- Summary
point: Sealed when we believed | Once we believe we are sealed by the Holy Spirit as the earnest, until redemption.
point: The earnest | The Spirit is the earnest of God, given in Christ, sealing us as His until the resurrection.
point: The surety | He gave His Son as surety and the Spirit as earnest.
point: The witness | You have the Spirit testifying within you. You know you are saved. Sealed.
point: His word | Nothing else matters. Not what we do. Not how we feel about it. Only that He gave us His word.
point: Not presumption | We who are saved know that we have the Holy Spirit testifying within us that we are the sons of God.

